menu "echo_ha (Charlie server)"

    config ECHO_HA_ENABLED
        bool "Connect to the Charlie server at boot"
        default y
        help
            Calls echo_ha_init() + echo_ha_start() from app_main(). The client
            keeps its own WebSocket (ws://<server>:9303/ws/echo) and retries in
            the background, so a boot without Wi-Fi is not fatal.

    config ECHO_HA_SERVER_IP
        string "Charlie server address"
        default ""
        help
            IPv4 address (or hostname) of the machine running the Charlie
            server. Empty means "not provisioned": echo_ha_start() logs a
            warning and the app can still set it at runtime with
            echo_ha_set_server() or the server's setServerIp command.

    config ECHO_HA_PORT
        int "Charlie server WebSocket port"
        range 1 65535
        default 9303
        help
            9303 is what the Arduino library and the Charlie server use. Only
            change it when the server is reconfigured to match.

    config ECHO_HA_WAKE_ACCURACY_PERMILLE
        int "Initial wake word accuracy (per mille)"
        range 0 1000
        default 900
        help
            Reported to the app and overridden by the server's
            setWakeUpWordAccuracy command (which is persisted in NVS). Kept as
            per mille so it fits a Kconfig int: 900 = 0.90.

    config ECHO_HA_TTS_END_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Silence that ends an assistant reply (ms)"
        range 200 10000
        default 1200
        help
            The protocol has no end-of-reply marker, so a gap in the binary
            audio frames closes the turn (ECHO_EVT_HA_TTS_END). Tune it against
            the server's chunk pacing: too small cuts long replies into several
            turns, too large delays the follow-up microphone.
endmenu
